WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:03.580
Thanks for giving me your cold while we were
together in Florida.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:04.680
I'm just kidding.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.680
NO THANKS!

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.290
What is the opposite of thanks?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.360
Shanks.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.780
Shanks for the cold, Hank.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.590
Anyway, it's Question Tuesday, the day that
I answer real questions from real Nerdfighters.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.590
Let's get right to it.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.170
Would you rather be a world famous banjo or
accordion player?

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.310
I'm gonna go with world famous banjo.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.390
I mean, being an accordion player would be
fun and everything, but I'd have to be human,

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.430
and all things being equal, I think I'd rather
be a banjo.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.220
Hey, how to you feel about the trailer for
the TFiOS movie leaking?

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.279
Kind of upset, mostly because the trailer
is not, like, an iPhone video of a low-res

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:30.279
screener.

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:31.900
It's in high definition, and it's beautiful.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.390
Also, it is debuting TOMORROW!

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.390
So you can see it then.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.180
You only have to wait like twenty-four hours.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.409
To hold you over, here is the world premiere
of a ten second teaser.

00:00:41.409 --> 00:00:51.079
Hazel [voiceover]: I can't tell you how thankful
I am for our little infinity.

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:53.239
That is what it really looks like.

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:54.929
FRENCH THE LLAMA I am excited!

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:56.499
I am still trying to make that into a thing.

00:00:56.499 --> 00:00:59.409
Hey speaking of movies, if a movie were to
be made about Dave Green, who do you think

00:00:59.409 --> 00:01:00.409
would play him?

00:01:00.409 --> 00:01:01.409
Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:01:01.409 --> 00:01:03.120
John, do you like Dave Green more than you
like Hank?

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.909
I'll tell you one thing: Dave never gave me
a horrible cold.

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:07.140
My daughter doesn't like pizza.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.229
Is she a monster?

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:11.080
Doesn't give me any pleasure to tell you this,
but yeah, I—I think she might be a monster.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.070
I mean, it could be lactose intolerance or
a gluten thing, but it—most likely monsterness.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.009
How excited are you about Esther's book coming
out today?

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:19.240
SO flipping excited.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.240
This book is wonderful.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.950
Please run, don't walk, to your nearest bookstore
to get a copy.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.030
There's also a link in the dooblydoo where
you can buy one on the Internet.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.990
In fact I'm going to do a live show tomorrow
to read from the book and talk more about

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:28.990
it, so I'll see you then.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.979
Have you ever thought about the fact that
guinea pigs are basically just meat potatoes?

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:35.880
Mmm, I prefer to think of potatoes as like
hairless, vegetarian guinea pigs.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.060
Who's your favorite member of One Direction?

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.580
I don't know, is there a nerdy one?

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.969
Hold on, I'll call Meredith and ask.

00:01:39.969 --> 00:01:42.409
Who's the nerdiest member of one direction?

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:44.609
All right, Niall.

00:01:44.609 --> 00:01:45.609
Thank you.

00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:46.719
Niall is my favorite member of One Direction.

00:01:46.719 --> 00:01:47.920
I don't know how to spell his name.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:48.920
Is it like the river?

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.249
Anyway, enough about how old I am.

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:51.249
Let's move on.

00:01:51.249 --> 00:01:52.320
Do you like your handwriting?

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.320
Not really.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.500
Everything I write looks like a ransom note
authored by a seven year old.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.289
I just read Franny and Zooey, and I can't
stop thinking about the quote "I'm sick of

00:01:58.289 --> 00:02:01.039
not having the courage to be an absolute nobody."

00:02:01.039 --> 00:02:02.039
What do you think of that?

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:03.110
That's one of my favorite lines in that book,
actually.

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:07.360
I think it takes tremendous courage to do
things that are worth doing rather than, like,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.340
worrying over whether you're going to be celebrated
for having done them.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:11.640
Chocolate chip cookies or Oreos?

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.070
I think you meant "and."

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.750
Chocolate chip cookies AND Oreos.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.170
And the answer to that is yes.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.200
If all the drawings you'd ever drawn came
to life and followed you around, how would

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.200
you react?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.400
I'd be like, "Man, I don't know if those are
horses or giraffes, but they sure are ugly."

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.770
Which U.S. president would you have play a
character in The Fault in our Stars movie?

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:32.890
All right, Gus is Obama; Hazel is Thomas Jefferson;
Hazel's mom and dad are respectively Millard

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:37.290
Fillmore and James K. Polk; Andrew Johnson
plays Van Houten; Isaac is played by Ulysses

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:42.740
S. Grant with no beard; Patrick-the-support-group-leader:
Jimmy Carter; Gus's mom: Martin Van Buren;

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.820
Gus's dad: Ronald Reagan; I cast the whole
movie!

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.680
Do you have any fishing boat proceeds for
2013?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.050
Sadly, no, still no fishing boat proceeds.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.540
My Tumblr generates lots of gifs, but no income.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:56.760
The fishing boat proceeds joke is now, like,
fully seven years old, and almost no one gets

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.120
it, but I assume that old Nerdfighters will
explain it to new Nerdfighters in comments.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.050
At what point am I considered a Nerdfighter?

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:04.830
If you wanna be a Nerdfighter, you probably
already are one.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:05.830
Favorite fairytale growing up?

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.360
The Emperor's New Clothes.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.360
Favorite museum in Amsterdam?

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.360
The Stedelijk.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.440
Do penguins have knees?

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.440
Yes.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.620
What color are your socks?

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.620
Green.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.810
And lastly, John, how many backflips can you
do?

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:21.360
So I think you just kinda—you go down like
this, and then you just—y'just kick your

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.750
legs way up, and you do a backflip.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:26.750
Hyuh!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:27.750
OAHH.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:28.750
Hiyehgy AHHHH.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:29.900
Oww hohoho.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:30.900
Haww.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:31.900
Zero.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.270
Zero, I can do zero backflips.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.890
Now Hank, I don't want to make excuses for
my inability to do a backflip, but I did get

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:41.280
pretty close to success even though, you know,
I have a massive cold that was caused by you.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.970
Hank, I'll see you on Friday, but before I
go, here is the teaser one last time.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:48.700
Hazel [voiceover]: I can't tell you how thankful
I am for our little infinity.

